Fix:

→ Left Rotation

   20(B)
  /    \
10(R)  30(R)

“Rotation is a tree restructuring technique used to maintain balance.
 In left rotation, the right child becomes the new root, and in right
 rotation, the left child becomes the new root. It ensures the height
 of the tree remains balanced.”

 👉 Middle element always comes on top
 👉 Left heavy → Right rotate
 👉 Right heavy → Left rotate
